      "writtenOn": "2018-01-10T21:19:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we were to write sge_array before we call init_sched_energy_costs, we could do something like:\n\nif (!cn) {\n    if (!sge_array[cpu][0]) {\n        pr_warn(\"Sched-energy-costs not available\\n\");\n        return;\n    }\n    continue;\n}\n\nThis would let non-DT platforms write whatever they want into sge_array, so long as it\u0027s done before we call here.\n\nIt will still be overridden by data from DT if supplied which is potentially problematic for debugging. Perhaps we could add a warning below for cases where you have populated sge_array *and* someone has put the sched-energy-costs node in the devicetree, it\u0027s bound to happen.",
      "range": {
